# Files listed here stay in the private repo but are never uploaded to the
# deployed site. Exclusion happens at the upload level, not by unlinking —
# an unlinked page is still reachable at its own URL.

# ── Non-public: the detailed UiPath Admin Shell case study ──────────────
# The .html shell is only 25 lines; the case study text lives in the .jsx.
# Excluding the shell alone would leave the full prose fetchable.
# All 7 frames/ diagrams are used by this page and by nothing else.
project-admin-shell.html
site/page-project-admin-shell.jsx
frames/

# ── Image masters, kept for re-export ───────────────────────────────────
# The 600px PNG originals for the About marquee. Kept in the repo as the
# sources to re-encode from when the photos change; the site serves the
# 400px WebP built from them, so the PNGs must never ship.
assets/about/*.png

# ── Archived design, kept for reference ─────────────────────────────────
# Components removed from live pages but preserved so the design can be
# recovered. Loaded by nothing. Must not deploy — password-gate.jsx still
# contains the old passcode string.
site/_archive/

# ── Not part of the site ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Developer control panel (themes, type scales). No longer loaded by any
# page. Kept in the repo; never published.
tweaks-panel.jsx
# Generic printable-document scaffold, unrelated to the portfolio.
doc-page.js
# Release Notes annotation explorations — design rounds, superseded.
site/release-notes-annotation-style-options.html
site/release-notes-annotation-styles-v2.html
site/release-notes-annotation-styles-v3.html

# ── Internal documentation ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# HANDOFF, MIGRATION_BRIEF, PROJECT_CONTEXT, DESIGN_SYSTEM and the uploads
# prompt file. No page loads a .md at runtime — every mention in the code
# is a comment — so excluding these changes nothing on screen.
*.md
